MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Phase 1 opener. Two migrations, each with its rollback, each ending with the
F-66 verification SELECT and — because a SELECT cannot stop an apply — a
DO block that RAISEs so a bad state cannot commit.

Both targets are F-62 class TRAP-BOTH: anon holds a named grant AND inherits
one through PUBLIC, so a single REVOKE of either kind succeeds and changes
nothing. Both files revoke both, and prove it.

Shown failing first on a scratch PostgreSQL 16.13 carrying production's own
default-privilege rule: 12 scenarios, 5 planted defects, all caught.

⚠ 20260910_0001 is NOT applicable yet. search_certificates is called from the
public unguarded /verify page (src/pages/VerifyCertificate.tsx:101), whose
handler renders a permission denial as "Certificate not found". Client first,
database second. The file carries an acknowledgement guard that refuses until
the client change has landed.

⚠ The method's precondition is unmet: D2's call-site inventory is not
delivered and the revocation list is not frozen. Recorded, not worked around.

