+    shipped 20260910_0001  07a830fdef34889dce7713e0dc89daac3b4d94d1a213ab0830422ac32de54e22
+    no_public variant      07a830fdef34889dce7713e0dc89daac3b4d94d1a213ab0830422ac32de54e22
+    no_anon variant        07a830fdef34889dce7713e0dc89daac3b4d94d1a213ab0830422ac32de54e22
+    too_wide variant       07a830fdef34889dce7713e0dc89daac3b4d94d1a213ab0830422ac32de54e22
+
+Identical. The control is unchanged; only the thing being controlled moved.
+
+── 3 · A DEFECT THE FIXTURE CAUGHT IN THIS FILE, BEFORE DELIVERY ──────────────
+
+The first draft looked the function up with
+
+    AND pg_get_function_identity_arguments(p.oid) = 'text, text, date'
+
+The fixture returned zero rows and the apply aborted with "does not exist".
+pg_get_function_identity_arguments INCLUDES PARAMETER NAMES when the function
+has them:
+
+    _name text, _course_title text, _issued_date date
+
+so the comparison could never match — on production either. Replaced with
+to_regprocedure('public.search_certificates(text, text, date)'), which resolves
+by TYPE signature, is independent of parameter names, and returns NULL rather
+than raising when the function is absent.
+
+This is the same class as the A4 correction in the TC-v3 unit. Recorded because
+a fixture that never catches anything is not doing its job.
